# Test accounts for the interactive test phase — EXAMPLE FILE. No real value belongs in it.
#
# Copy this file to `{{credentialsPath}}` — the path `harness.config.json` holds in
# `qa.credentialsPath` — fill one block in there per account, and keep that copy out of
# version control; `autonomous-sdlc-harness init` adds the ignore line for it. Only the
# *path* is configuration. A credential value never is: it does not go into
# `harness.config.json`, a plan, a review finding, a test report or a commit message, and
# this example file is the only one of the pair that is committed.
#
# Key names are the harness's own and are prefixed `HARNESS_QA_<n>_`. They were renamed to
# that prefix when the harness was extracted from the project it grew in, so if you are
# carrying accounts over from an earlier runner, rename the keys rather than the reader.
#
# Add accounts by incrementing <n>. The phase reserves one account per concurrent session
# and releases it at the end, so give it at least as many as you expect to run at once —
# two sessions signed in as one user interfere with each other in ways that look like
# product defects.

# Use accounts that exist only to be tested with. Never a real person's, and never one with
# elevated privileges: a test that needs those reports itself blocked instead.

# The identifier the sign-in form is given. Which form that is comes from `qa.authProvider`.
HARNESS_QA_1_EMAIL=
# The account's password, for that same form. This is the one line the whole file exists to keep
# out of version control.
HARNESS_QA_1_PASSWORD=
# The account's own identifier in the product, for a test that has to recognise its own data —
# its posts, its messages — among everyone else's.
HARNESS_QA_1_USER_ID=
# The name the interface shows for this account, so a test can assert it is signed in as the
# account it reserved rather than a leftover session.
HARNESS_QA_1_DISPLAY_NAME=

# The second account, and so on. Uncomment and fill in as many as you need.
# HARNESS_QA_2_EMAIL=
# HARNESS_QA_2_PASSWORD=
# HARNESS_QA_2_USER_ID=
# HARNESS_QA_2_DISPLAY_NAME=
